\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Backgrounds and symmetry}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Which changes of labels preserve equations, Gaussian expectations
and a chosen marginal? Endpoint transport and coherent edge reversals
control the incidence map; the half-turn of the alternating cycle gives
a concrete action. Perfect pairings and a chosen retained split then
transport the operators and observable functionals. The finite-carrier,
[duality](fdip-001F), [split-map](fdip-001T) and
[normalized-functional](fdip-0021) conventions are assumed.}

\p{For positive real precisions, the proved
[Gaussian integral](fdip-002T) and [marginal theorem](fdip-000E)
identify the transported functionals with normalized laws. Fixed labels,
broken weights and nonstable partitions give different failures.
An intrinsic trace ratio separates two cycles under a broader scaling
comparison, while general quadratic isometries can transport a law
without preserving its reference pairing or projection.}

